  "analysis": [
    {
      "label": "Context",
      "text": "Only five minutes in, with the score 0–0, Belgium had started on the front foot. Players pushed forward left space behind the Belgian midfield for a counter from deep."
    },
    {
      "label": "Key moment",
      "text": "Al-Owairan took the ball in the Saudi half and went straight at goal. Beating the first challenge at pace meant the Belgian midfield was already chasing from behind."
    },
    {
      "label": "Defenders' choices",
      "text": "Belgians came in one or two at a time and never stopped the run early with a foul. Each tackle that missed left the next defender facing a player at full speed."
    },
    {
      "label": "Why it worked",
      "text": "Pace and a direct line kept the defence retreating all the way. By the time Al-Owairan reached the box, Preud'homme was left facing the attacker almost alone."
